# Public surface — no private maintainer environment

Cretli on GitHub is **public**. README, docs, UI copy, comments, tests, fixtures, screenshots, and changelog examples must not identify the maintainer’s private clients, machines, or network.

## Never put in committed or user-visible files

- Real commercial site names, client brands, or sibling WWW projects from a private workspace
- Home directories, usernames, Synology/Obsidian paths, WSL-only hostnames
- Private LAN IPs (`192.168.*`, `10.*`) as examples in docs or UI (use `your-pc` / `127.0.0.1` / `localhost`)
- Real widget installation IDs, API keys, or machine names

## Use instead

Generic fiction: `my-app`, `acme`, `example.com`, `your-pc`, `https://your-pc:3011`.

This rule is for **this repository**. Do not document private client names in the rule text or in comments.
